{%- comment -%}
  Resolves a formula name ("Velvet") to that product's real URL.

  Needed because the products are not handled by their short names: Velvet is
  /products/velvet-foaming-facial-cleanser, so every hand-built
  "/products/{{ name | downcase }}" link in this theme was a 404.

  Matches on the first segment of the handle rather than `contains`, so a name
  cannot pick up a bundle or a longer product that merely mentions it.
  Falls back to the short handle, which is what the old links did, so a product
  that genuinely is handled that way still works.

  Usage: {%- render 'product-url-by-name', name: 'Velvet' -%}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign key = name | downcase | strip
  assign found = ''
  for p in collections.all.products
    assign stem = p.handle | split: '-' | first
    if stem == key
      assign found = p.url
      break
    endif
  endfor
  if found == blank
    assign found = '/products/' | append: key
  endif
  echo found
-%}
